---
import MovieFlexLegalLayout from "../layouts/MovieFlexLegalLayout.astro";
---

<MovieFlexLegalLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="How MovieFlex uses browser storage and third-party requests."
  eyebrow="BROWSER STORAGE"
>
  <h2>Cookies used by MovieFlex</h2>
  <p>
    The current MovieFlex interface does not intentionally set browser cookies
    for analytics or advertising. It uses browser <code>localStorage</code> for
    its watchlist and to remember your essential-only privacy choice.
  </p>
  <h2>Essential local storage</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>movieflex-watchlist-v2</code> stores the movie entries you save on
      this device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>movieflex-storage-choice-v1</code> records your essential-only
      storage choice.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These entries are stored in this browser, not in a MovieFlex user account.
    Clearing the browser's site data removes them. If browser storage is
    blocked, the watchlist may last only for the current visit.
  </p>
  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Poster and logo assets may be requested from TMDB's image service. Opening
    TMDB, JustWatch, or a streaming provider takes you to a third-party site
    that may use cookies, local storage, or similar technologies under its own
    policy.
  </p>
  <h2>Managing storage</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear site data from your browser settings. You can also clear your
    saved MovieFlex watchlist from the app's watchlist panel or the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy-settings">Privacy settings</a> page.
  </p>
  <h2>Policy changes</h2>
  <p>
    If analytics, advertising, or additional storage technologies are added,
    this policy and the available controls should be updated before they are
    used.
  </p>
</MovieFlexLegalLayout>
